^SAMPLE = GSM2365783
!Sample_title = RNA_L21_2
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM2365783
!Sample_status = Public on May 17 2017
!Sample_submission_date = Oct 29 2016
!Sample_last_update_date = May 15 2019
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Sort-purified (CD8/Thy1.1) TCR SV40-I CD8 T cells isolated D21 from early malignant lesions replicate#2
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = strain: C57BL/6
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cd8 t cell status: TCR SV40-I transgenic CD8 T cells
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = disease state: early malignant liver lesions
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = CD8 T cells were FACS-sorted straight into Trizol tube and stored at -80°C until all samples were collected. RNA from sorted cells was extracted using RNeasy mini kit (Qiagen) according to instructions provided by the manufacturer. After ribogreen quantification and quality control of Agilent BioAnalyzer, 6-15 ng of total RNA underwent amplification (12 cycles) using the SMART-seq V4 (Clonetech) ultralow input RNA kit for sequencing. 10ng of amplified cDNA was used to prepare Illumina hiseq libraries with the Kapa DNA library preparation chemistry (Kapa Biosystems) using 8 cycles of PCR. Samples were barcoded and run on a Hiseq 2500 1T in a 50bp/50bp Paired end run, using the TruSeq SBS Kit v3 (Illumina).  An average of 51 million paired reads were generated per sample and the percent of mRNA bases was 62.5% on average.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = 10ng of amplified cDNA was used to prepare Illumina hiseq libraries with the Kapa DNA library preparation chemistry (Kapa Biosystems) using 8 cycles of PCR. Samples were barcoded and run on a Hiseq 2500 1T in a 50bp/50bp Paired end run, using the TruSeq SBS Kit v3 (Illumina).
!Sample_data_processing = Base trimming and quality filtering using TrimGalore! v0.4.0, powered by CutAdapt v1.8.1 and FastQC v0.11.3 using paired and fastqc options
!Sample_data_processing = Paired-end alignment using STAR v2.4.0f1 and default parameters
!Sample_data_processing = Conversion of sam to bam file and ordering of aligned reads using SAMtools v0.1.18
!Sample_data_processing = Counting of reads aligning to transcripts using the summarizeOverlaps function of the R package GenomicAlignments v1.2.2 and GenomicRanges v1.18.4
!Sample_data_processing = Library-size normalized read counts were calculated using DESeq2 v1.6.3
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: mm10
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Text file containing DESeq size-factor normalized counts per gene. First column indicates gene Entrez ID, second column indicates normalized count value
